# Cursor rules — FilsPay monorepo
# Rewritten 2026-10-30. The full conventions are in CLAUDE.md; the earlier
# version of this file hid real bugs (docs/bugs/points/60-ai-rule-files-preserve-bugs.md).

# Authority
# ADRs in docs/adr/ are the rules. ARCHITECTURE, HANDOVER, CHANGELOG, code
# comments and tests are claims: verify them in the code.

# Money
# Integer fils, 1 BD = 1000 fils (ADR-0001), never cents. parseBhdToFils in,
# formatBhd out, applyRateFils for basis points, allocateRemainder for splits.
# No parseFloat / toFixed / * 100 / float32 / float64 on money. BIGINT columns.

# Time
# Settlement business day = Asia/Bahrain midnight to midnight (UTC+3).

# Security
# OTPs, payment-link tokens, invite codes, sessions and API keys come from
# node:crypto, never Math.random(). Scope every query by the authenticated
# merchant. Admin routes declare roles explicitly. Impersonation is read-only.

# Concurrency
# Read-then-write = one atomic conditional UPDATE, or FOR UPDATE held to the end.

# Migrations
# New files only, numbered above the highest. Never edit an applied migration.

# Tests
# A failing test first for every fix. A test that pins a bug is corrected
# with the fix, with a comment. Fresh database. Go: -p 1 and DATABASE_URL set
# (without it the DB-backed tests skip themselves and the run still says ok).
